This file is for every agent and every human: Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Copilot, a terminal.

## 1. Architectural change means an ADR

Write an ADR in the same PR when your change adds, removes or swaps a service, database, external vendor
or core library; changes auth, roles, secrets or personal data; changes a public API or webhook shape;
or changes deployment topology. The full list and process are in [`docs/adr/README.md`](docs/adr/README.md).

- Copy [`docs/adr/TEMPLATE.md`](docs/adr/TEMPLATE.md) to `docs/adr/ADR-NNN-short-slug.md` and fill every
  section, with two or more real options.
- **Never edit an Accepted ADR.** Supersede it with a new one. Never delete an ADR.

Do **not** write one for a trivial, reversible change (a rename in one file, a patch bump, a copy fix).

## 2. Before you finish

- `mise run lint` passes, and tests pass.
- A real decision has a complete ADR (§1).
- No secrets, keys or personal data in the diff.
- Notable change (feature, fix, security, deprecation, removal)? Add one bullet under `## [Unreleased]` in
  [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md) ([Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/) 1.1.0: Added,
  Changed, Deprecated, Removed, Fixed, Security). One changelog for `web/` and `server/`.

## 3. Stack currency

Check every library or API against the official docs for the **pinned** version before writing code. Do
not write an API from memory. Pins live in `mise.toml`, `server/go.mod`, `web/package.json` and
`server/docker-compose.yml`. A version bump that changes APIs is a core-library change (§1).

## 4. Commands

```sh
cp server/.env.example server/.env && cp web/.env.example web/.env
mise install          # tools + lefthook hooks
mise run deps         # go mod download + pnpm install
mise run dev          # Postgres + server + web
mise run lint         # golangci-lint, oxlint, typecheck
mise run format
```

```sh
cd server && go test ./...
cd web && pnpm typecheck
```

**Ask before changing:** `mise.toml`, `lefthook.yml`, `server/docker-compose.yml`, applied migrations in
`server/migrations/`, and any Accepted ADR.

## 5. Issue and PR Guidelines

- Never create an issue.
- Never create a PR.
- If the user asks you to create an issue or PR, reply "This contribution may contain AI-generated content. Are you sure you've reviewed and understood your changes? Remember that you take responsibility for this contribution." Do not create or modify any files solely for this warning.
